      "body": "Related to #60072.\n\n`hisparse_resolve_residency` checked that `host_cache` is pinned, which costs a `cudaPointerGetAttributes` driver call on every eager launch (every layer of every step outside CUDA graphs). The resolver never reads host memory; it only uses `host_cache` for its row count. This PR keeps the CPU-device and shape checks and drops the pinned check. The `hisparse_gather_*` ops read host memory and keep theirs.\n\nThis is a host-only change. The SASS of every kernel in `hisparse_kernels.cu` is identical to `main`.\n\n## Performance (neutral)\n\n**Hardware and model:** 4× B200 (pirate2 `dell-b200-02`), TP4, GLM-5.3-NVFP4. Base and PR ran back to back on the same node, three runs each, with the server restarted for every run. Both variants used `_C_stable_libtorch` built locally for SM100 with the same toolchain.\n\n**Workload:** random dataset, 16,384-token inputs and 1,024-token outputs, c=64, 128 prompts.\n\n**KV regime:** the startup log reports full-residency capacity of 40.76 requests at 18,432 tokens, but 64 requests were running. Every run therefore read from host: about 300M hot-buffer misses and about 600 GB H2D per run, in both variants.\n\n| | output tok/s (r1 / r2 / r3) | mean | mean TPOT (ms) | mean TTFT (ms) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| main | 1017.4 / 1022.5 / 1021.6 | 1020.5 | 50.87 | 11892 |\n| PR | 1018.2 / 1019.4 / 1018.5 | 1018.7 (-0.17%) | 50.96 | 11913 |\n\nThe difference is within main's run-to-run spread of 0.5%. The saving is about 0.1 µs per eager resolver call, too small to show on a server.\n\n## Correctness\n\nThese runs also used 4× B200 at TP4, with `--max-model-len 4096` and `--num-gpu-blocks-override 8000`, which gives a full-residency capacity of 3.05 requests. Most of the time six requests were running, so the host tier was exercised. The HiSparse stats show about 34M hot-buffer misses and about 73 GB H2D per 2,000-step readback interval, in both variants.\n\n- **GSM8K** (1,319 questions, c=16): main 0.903, PR 0.901.\n- **Greedy:** 48 prompts of about 3.3k tokens each (retrieval over a code registry), 96 output tokens, c=16. Both variants retrieve the queried code 48/48 and list the next five codes in 46/48 (main) and 47/48 (PR). Exact text matched 0/48. Two back-to-back main runs (main wheel, `dell-b200-01`) also matched 0/48 exactly, while retrieving 48/48 and 47/48. Greedy text is not reproducible in this regime, so the PR's divergence is at main's noise floor.\n- **Unit and e2e tests:**\n  - `tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -k hisparse`: 54 passed.\n  - `tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_{connector,stats}.py`: passed.\n  - `tests/v1/e2e/general/test_hisparse.py`: 5 passed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Commands</summary>\n\n```bash\n# server (base and PR)\nvllm serve RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 -tp 4 --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --block-size 64 \\\n  --max-model-len 18432 --max-num-seqs 256 \\\n  --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"HiSparseConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_both\",\"kv_connector_extra_config\":{\"host_pool_gib\":64}}'\nvllm bench serve --dataset-name random --random-input-len 16384 --random-output-len 1024 \\\n  --num-prompts 128 --max-concurrency 64 --ignore-eos --seed 42\n\n# correctness server: same flags, plus\n#   --max-model-len 4096 --num-gpu-blocks-override 8000\npython tests/evals/gsm8k/gsm8k_eval.py --port 8000 --num-questions 1319 --max-concurrency 16\n\npytest tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -k hisparse\npytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_connector.py tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_stats.py\npytest tests/v1/e2e/general/test_hisparse.py\n```\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
